1
00:00:00,128 --> 00:00:07,338
The job is triage under alert fatigue.
Analysts were losing the incident across the SIEM, the mailbox, and the ticket.

2
00:00:07,418 --> 00:00:12,216
Access is role-based.
A failed sign-in stays on this screen, so the queue is never exposed.

3
00:00:12,296 --> 00:00:17,891
Alex is the tier-2 analyst.
The home screen is the queue, and the red badge is the critical count.

4
00:00:17,971 --> 00:00:23,580
Severity is the first prioritization cut.
Low stays in the product, but it does not sit on top of an active intrusion.

5
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:29,352
Critical is the interrupt.
The filter is a product choice: fewer cards, faster judgment.

6
00:00:29,432 --> 00:00:35,682
Owner, source, and asset are on the card.
The next click should be a decision, not a lookup in another tool.

7
00:00:35,762 --> 00:00:41,384
One search returns the incident, the alert, and the indicator.
That is the response to switching between tools.

8
00:00:41,464 --> 00:00:47,652
Ledger Fox is one campaign.
The invoice mail, the beacon, and the network sessions are linked here instead of in a spreadsheet.

9
00:00:47,732 --> 00:00:53,487
Ownership is explicit. Priya leads the case.
The notes stay on the incident, so the handoff is not a side channel.

10
00:00:53,567 --> 00:00:59,616
The list is what a lead scans.
Severity, status, owner, and how many alerts sit under the case.

11
00:00:59,696 --> 00:01:06,018
This question does not spend a model.
It is answered from the alert store and labeled database, so a lookup stays cheap and checkable.

12
00:01:06,098 --> 00:01:12,568
Language summaries use a low-cost model.
Only campaign and correlation questions earn the expensive models. Cost and trust were separate decisions.

13
00:01:12,648 --> 00:01:19,118
Handoff has types, not a single chat box.
A note, a question, an escalation to tier 3, and a resolution.

14
00:01:19,198 --> 00:01:25,668
These are the outcomes for a SOC manager.
Detect time, response time, and the false-positive rate. Volume alone is not progress.

15
00:01:25,748 --> 00:01:31,335
Indicators stay with the campaign.
The invoice site, the billing address, and the beacon address are in one place.

16
00:01:31,415 --> 00:01:37,608
The graph is the correlation analysts used to do by hand.
A relationship should be visible without opening a second console.

17
00:01:37,688 --> 00:01:43,592
Reports are split by the reader.
Management gets the executive summary. Every role does not get the same document.

18
00:01:43,672 --> 00:01:49,272
Tier 3 gets the incident write-up and the threat summary.
Same underlying records, a different job to be done.

19
00:01:49,352 --> 00:01:55,552
The cadence goes to the CISO and the SOC manager.
The analyst is not the person who should remember the export.

20
00:01:55,632 --> 00:02:00,832
The loop is triage, correlate, hand off, measure, and report.
Each screen exists because it removes a wait or a tool switch.
